---
import Base from '../../layouts/Base.astro';
import SectionLabel from '../../components/SectionLabel.astro';
---

<Base
  title="Will It Fit Privacy Policy"
  description="Will It Fit's privacy policy: the app collects no data, makes no network requests at all, and every scan stays on your device."
>
  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-8 py-section">
      <SectionLabel label="will it fit · privacy policy" />
      <h1 class="mt-6 text-page-h1 text-text-primary max-w-prose">
        Will It Fit collects nothing, and sends nothing.
      </h1>
      <p class="mt-6 text-card-body text-text-secondary max-w-prose">
        Last updated: August 2026
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-8 section-divider"></div>

  <section>
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-page px-8 py-section max-w-prose space-y-8">
      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Data collection</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Will It Fit doesn't collect your data. There are no accounts, no sign-in, no analytics
          SDKs, no advertising identifiers, and no crash-reporting service. Everything the app
          produces, every scan, every measurement, every saved space and every result, is created
          and stored entirely on your device.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          The app makes no network requests of its own at all. Not one. It is built to work with
          the phone in airplane mode, in an underground car park, or in a shop with no signal,
          because that is exactly where people need it. The only network traffic associated with
          the app is Apple's own, when you make or restore a purchase, which is described below.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Camera and LiDAR</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Scanning uses your iPhone's camera and its LiDAR depth sensor, with your permission. The
          camera feed and the depth data are processed live on your device to build a 3D mesh of
          the space or object you are pointing at, and that mesh is immediately reduced to the
          measurements the app actually needs. No photograph, video, or camera frame is ever
          uploaded anywhere, because the app has nowhere to upload it to.
        </p>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          When you save a space to your library, the app keeps a single still thumbnail of it so
          the saved card has a picture on it. That thumbnail lives on your device with everything
          else and is only ever shown to you.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Storage</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Saved spaces, passages, fit-check history, your settings, and your purchase status are
          stored locally on your device using standard iOS storage, including the Keychain for
          purchase status. There is no cloud sync, no server, and no way for anyone, including the
          developer, to reach any of it remotely. Deleting the app deletes the data with it.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Share cards</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          The app can render a result as an image you can share. That image is generated on your
          device and handed to the standard iOS share sheet. Nothing is posted anywhere on your
          behalf, and the app is not told what you do with the image after that. Where it goes is
          entirely your choice, and whichever app or service you send it to handles it under its
          own privacy policy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Purchases</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          The lifetime unlock is a one-time purchase processed entirely through Apple's In-App
          Purchase system. Payment details are handled by Apple and are never seen by Will It Fit
          or its developer. The app stores only a yes-or-no record of whether the unlock has been
          bought, in your device's Keychain, so that reinstalling doesn't lose it. Restoring a
          purchase asks Apple, not us.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Airline and parcel data</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          The cabin and checked baggage limits, and the courier parcel sizes, that Quick Measure
          compares your bag against are bundled inside the app as a plain data file. Looking one
          up is a local lookup. Nothing about your bag, your airline, or your trip is transmitted.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Children</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Will It Fit does not knowingly collect information from anyone, including children,
          because it does not collect information from anyone.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Changes to this policy</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          If this policy ever changes, the update will be posted on this page with a new "last
          updated" date above.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div>
        <h2 class="mono-label">Contact</h2>
        <p class="mt-3 text-card-body text-text-secondary">
          Questions about this policy: <a href="mailto:ai@stewart-burton.com" class="text-accent hover:underline">ai@stewart-burton.com</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
